<title>UK: Kvaerner wins $23 mln Japan ship contract.</title>
<headline>Kvaerner wins $23 mln Japan ship contract.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Anglo-Norwegian construction and engineering group Kvaerner ASA said on Thursday its Kvaerner Klevin subsidiary had won a contract from Japan's Sanko Steamship Co, to build an anchor handling and tug vessel worth $23 million.  </p>
<p>The delivery of the vessel is due in May 1999.</p>
<p>The 'KMAR 404' ship, designed by Kvaerner Maritime, has been developed to service rigs in medium to deep waters, as well as production ships.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4366</p>
